{
  "notes": "Cinematic, Eb lydian, 80 BPM, a lilting triplet feel. A soft phase-distortion electric piano turning a broken chord over in eighth-note triplets like a home-movie loop (a slow tape wow on its pitch), a dusty granular cloud holding each chord's third and seventh, the player's breathy flute on the Smart Keys (mono, glide, delayed vibrato, triplet echoes), and a CR-78 rhythm box ticking quarter notes like the archive's clock. The lydian II (F over Eb) floats every cadence home. Scenes: A a remembered fragment over Imaj7 and II; B the loop on I vi I II; C the bass rises through vi I to a II(sus4) that resolves; D the fragment again, II back to I, in a bigger, darker room. COLOR is the tape's age (dark: dust and dull tone; bright: a vivid recall), MOTION the wow and the grain drift, SPACE the room and the echoes, ENERGY brings in the piano, then the clock, then the snare and fills. All material is original.",
